{
  "id": "03041_iyagaru",
  "headword": "{嫌|いや}がる",
  "reading": "いやがる",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to dislike, to be unwilling",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "godan",
    "ending": "る",
    "stem": "{嫌|いや}が"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to dislike, to hate",
      "explanation": "To show signs of disliking something; to express unwillingness or reluctance. Used when describing someone else's feelings of aversion."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "03041_iyagaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{子供|こども}が{野菜|やさい}を{嫌|いや}がる。",
      "english": "The child dislikes vegetables.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03041_iyagaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{猫|ねこ}は{水|みず}を{嫌|いや}がることが{多|おお}い。",
      "english": "Cats often dislike water.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03041_iyagaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{人前|ひとまえ}で{話|はな}すのを{嫌|いや}がっている。",
      "english": "He is reluctant to speak in front of people.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: Xを{嫌|いや}がる.\n\nGRAMMAR POINT:\n{嫌|いや}がる is formed from {嫌|いや} (disliked) + がる (to show signs of). The がる suffix indicates observable behavior showing an internal feeling, used when describing others' feelings (not your own).\n\nASPECT: {嫌|いや}がっている indicates ongoing reluctance or aversion.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {嫌|いや}がる: to show dislike (observable behavior)\n- {嫌|きら}う: to dislike (internal feeling, can be used for self)\n- {嫌|いや}だ: to dislike (direct statement of own feelings)",
